# Concrete natural tensor facts for the marked critical pair

The literal SL₃(2) × S₃ external tensor representation is faithful and has no
transvections. Its point radical has fixed codimension four. Each nontrivial
proper radical subgroup has order two and fixed codimension two; each
nonidentity radical element has displacement rank two. On the fixed space of
any such proper subgroup, the radical's displacements escape every line.

These finite model results supply the representation-theoretic inputs to the
marked critical-pair argument for Aschbacher–Smith 13.8.21(1), printed p.957.
The ambient critical-pair construction and its source hypotheses belong to
the assembly owner.
-/
